==Aftermath==
After the election, in April 1998, Artūras Paulauskas and his campaign team formed a political party, the [[New Union (Social Liberals)]]. This party received the second largest share of the vote in the [[2000 Lithuanian parliamentary election|2000 parliamentary election]], after the social democratic coalition led by Algirdas Brazauskas and the [[Democratic Labour Party of Lithuania]].

